From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:34:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btbcm: Treat the BCM4350C5 default address as
 invalid

The iPhone 6s Plus's BCM4350C5 reports 43:50:C5:00:1F:AC, before and
after its Patchram loads, unless the host sets an address. It was taken
as the controller's own, so hci_bcm never set
HCI_QUIRK_USE_BDADDR_PROPERTY and the address the boot loader puts in
local-bd-address (the unit's, from the Apple device tree) went unused.
Add it to the known default addresses.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/bluetooth/btbcm.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btbcm.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btbcm.c
index baba42563..e9af5a4f2 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btbcm.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btbcm.c
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@
 #define BDADDR_BCM4330B1 (&(bdaddr_t) {{0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0xb1, 0x30, 0x43}})
 #define BDADDR_BCM4334B0 (&(bdaddr_t) {{0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0xb0, 0x34, 0x43}})
 #define BDADDR_BCM4345C5 (&(bdaddr_t) {{0xac, 0x1f, 0x00, 0xc5, 0x45, 0x43}})
+#define BDADDR_BCM4350C5 (&(bdaddr_t) {{0xac, 0x1f, 0x00, 0xc5, 0x50, 0x43}})
 #define BDADDR_BCM4355C0 (&(bdaddr_t) {{0xac, 0x1f, 0x00, 0xc0, 0x55, 0x43}})
 #define BDADDR_BCM4355C1 (&(bdaddr_t) {{0x93, 0x76, 0x00, 0xc1, 0x55, 0x43}})
 #define BDADDR_BCM43341B (&(bdaddr_t) {{0xac, 0x1f, 0x00, 0x1b, 0x34, 0x43}})
@@ -123,6 +124,9 @@ int btbcm_check_bdaddr(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 	 * The address AA:AA:AA:AA:AA:AA indicates a BCM43430A1 controller
 	 * with no configured address.
 	 *
+	 * The address 43:50:C5:00:1F:AC indicates a BCM4350C5 controller
+	 * with no configured address.
+	 *
 	 * The address 43:55:C0:00:1F:AC indicates a BCM4355C0 controller
 	 * with no configured address.
 	 *
@@ -136,6 +140,7 @@ int btbcm_check_bdaddr(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 	    !bacmp(&bda->bdaddr, BDADDR_BCM4330B1) ||
 	    !bacmp(&bda->bdaddr, BDADDR_BCM4334B0) ||
 	    !bacmp(&bda->bdaddr, BDADDR_BCM4345C5) ||
+	    !bacmp(&bda->bdaddr, BDADDR_BCM4350C5) ||
 	    !bacmp(&bda->bdaddr, BDADDR_BCM4355C0) ||
 	    !bacmp(&bda->bdaddr, BDADDR_BCM4355C1) ||
 	    !bacmp(&bda->bdaddr, BDADDR_BCM43430A0) ||
